\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Related Tetouan studies. Results are transcribed from the repository review and comparison CSV; RMSE/MAE use its reported kW scale and MAPE is percent. These are not a common benchmark. NR denotes unavailable configuration-specific evidence.}}{3}{table.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Whole-year descriptive statistics of the original ten-minute observations (T01). Blank source units are left unspecified.}}{4}{table.caption.4}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Implemented feature groups and prediction-time availability. The target-hour weather values are observed rather than forecast.}}{10}{table.caption.13}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Chronological partitions after history-related row removal (T02). All dates are in 2017; end times are 23:00.}}{12}{table.caption.14}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Expanding-window h24 cross-validation (T02). Training starts on 8 January at 23:00 in every fold; validation begins at 00:00 and ends at 23:00.}}{12}{table.caption.15}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces November validation, h24: seasonal baselines, default regressors and RF-P1 (T04). RMSE/MAE are in kW; MAPE is percent.}}{15}{table.caption.17}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Default-model development CV, h24 (T05). SD is the sample standard deviation over five folds, not a confidence interval. Errors in kW; MAPE in percent.}}{17}{table.caption.20}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Default h24 RMSE by temporal fold (T05), in kW. Models are ordered by mean fold RMSE; fold boundaries are given in Table~\ref {tab:folds}.}}{18}{table.caption.21}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Search spaces shared by both horizons and both target formulations (T06). Budgets are per model formulation, not per parameter. Integer limits are inclusive as displayed.}}{19}{table.9}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Selected h24 hyperparameters from best\_params.json. Estimator-wrapper prefixes are omitted; floating values are rounded to six decimals. Both target formulations were searched independently.}}{20}{table.10}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Tuned h24 development CV (T07). RMSE and its SD are in kW. Improvement compares each row with the absolute default model of that family; $\Delta $ rows combine tuning with a target change.}}{21}{table.caption.23}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Feature ablation with fixed D-selected hyperparameters: mean CV RMSE in kW (T09). Missing entries were not run because the residual base is absent.}}{23}{table.caption.25}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Development CV horizon comparison (T10), RMSE in kW: best formulation within each family chosen separately per horizon. LR, DT, RF and XGB use residual targets; SVR uses the absolute target.}}{24}{table.caption.27}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces December h24 evaluation (T08), ordered by observed RMSE. The CV-selected model is SVR-tuned. This ordering does not redefine selection. RMSE/MAE in kW; skill is RMSE reduction against Naive-24h.}}{26}{table.caption.29}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces December h1 evaluation (T08), ordered by observed RMSE. The CV-selected model is SVR-tuned. This ordering does not redefine selection. RMSE/MAE in kW; skill is RMSE reduction against Naive-24h.}}{27}{table.caption.30}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Five largest daily MAEs for the selected h24 SVR (T08). Bias is prediction minus actual; all numerical columns are in kW.}}{28}{table.caption.34}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Four RF diagnostic settings (T12). These rows differ in task and test distribution and must not be treated as a controlled leakage-effect estimate. Errors in kW.}}{32}{table.caption.37}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Post-final RF search diagnostic: 20 candidates per CV strategy (T12b). Optimism is $100(\mathrm {RMSE}_{test}/\mathrm {RMSE}_{CV}-1)$. Errors in kW.}}{33}{table.caption.39}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Recorded h24 refit and whole-test prediction durations for selected representative models (T08). Hardware and thread configuration are not recorded in this table; timings are descriptive.}}{34}{table.caption.40}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Recorded experiment dependencies from requirements.txt; Python 3.12 is specified by the repository. These are recorded pins, not a newly reproduced environment.}}{38}{table.caption.42}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Supplementary default CV variability for all four metrics (T05); mean $\pm $ sample SD. RMSE/MAE in kW, MAPE in percent.}}{39}{table.caption.43}%
